<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Claudius Marcellus (consul 166 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 148 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Claudius Marcellus, grandson of the conqueror of Syracuse, was a Roman general who was consul three times, in 166, 155 and 152 BCE. As governor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> he founded Corduba, the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, which became the seat of the governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-ulterior">Hispania Ulterior</a>, and he negotiated a peace with the Celtiberians in 152 BCE.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Governors based at Corduba, founded by <b>Marcus Claudius Marcellus</b> in the 2nd century BCE, commanded armies and collected tribute from Iberian and Phoenician towns.</blockquote><a href="/state/hispania-ulterior">Hispania Ulterior</a></li></ul></section>
